course: dictionary
lesson: 4934
title: Impetigo: a catching skin infection
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Impetigo is a word you may meet in health lessons. Read the words around it to work out its meaning: «Impetigo is a skin infection spread by touch and common in mat sports.» The clues are skin, infection and spread by touch.
explain: An infection is an illness caused by germs getting into the body. Spread by touch means it passes from one person to another when they touch. So impetigo is catching, and it can move from person to person.
explain: The sentence also describes the sores: «sores that dry into golden crusts». A sore is a break in the skin that hurts or looks raw. A crust is the hard layer that forms over a sore as it dries.
fact: Impetigo is a common skin infection caused by bacteria, a kind of germ.
fact: It gives red sores that burst and form golden-yellow crusts, often on the face and hands.
fact: It is mostly seen in young children, and it is very catching by touching sores, towels or toys.
fact: A doctor may give cream or medicine, and washing hands and not sharing towels helps stop it spreading.
fact: The NHS says to stay off school until the sores crust over or 48 hours after starting antibiotics.
exercise: «Impetigo is a skin infection spread by touch.» What is impetigo? | *A common skin infection caused by germs | A kind of cold that makes you sneeze | A sweet, golden drink | A broken bone in the arm
exercise: The red sores of impetigo dry into what? | Blue bubbles | Hard white stones | Long, thin lines | *Golden-yellow crusts
exercise: Why might a child with impetigo need to stay off school? | Because it stops them from reading | Because the school is closed for cleaning all year | Because it makes them grow very tall | *Because it can spread to others by touch
test: Which of these helps stop impetigo spreading? | Sharing the same drink bottle | Touching the sores to see how they feel | *Washing hands and not sharing towels | Sharing towels with friends
test: In health lessons, «catching» means what? | Growing in a garden | Able to be caught in a net | *Able to pass from one person to another | Very quick at running
exam: Your friend has impetigo sores. Which is the safest thing to do? | Share your towel with them to help | *Wash your hands after touching them and use your own towel | Lick the sores to clean them | Touch their sores to check how they feel
